KG42.register("rules-a6dddf61c61c572cafcd3308",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R010","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The local energy product includes excess energy offered to adjacent H-MGs and energy acquired from neighboring H-MGs to cover power shortages. Scope: Proposed retail market; energy exchanges among H-MGs connected to the same network.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Proposed retail market; energy exchanges among H-MGs connected to the same network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy product includes excess energy offered to adjacent H-MGs and energy acquired from neighboring H-MGs to cover power shortages. Scope: Proposed retail market; energy exchanges among H-MGs connected to the same network.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. H-MG concept","anchor_text":"i.e., generators try to maximize their proﬁt while consumers look hin after minimizing their operati","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In a similar manner to microgrid interoperability, several H-MGs, connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform, can sell their excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or supply their power shortage through neighbours instead of purchasing energy from retailers. For a microgrid to be able to do this, it is necessary to have an energy management system (EMS) to make decisions in day-ahead and real-time operation. In this paper, every H-MG is assumed to have a home energy management system (HEMS) which is able to send/receive signals to/from a market operator, as explained later in detail. HEMS could functionally be able to predict local load demand, renewable generation, and demand flexibility, and to generate scenarios for the stochastic parameters. The HEMS is physically connected to generation, storage, and DR resources in the H-MG to operate them accordingly, and to the market operator to participate in energy trading. Therefore, HEMS is an integral part of the H-MG concept and the proposed market mechanism in this paper."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No decision or design variable is defined for this product in the supplied source passage or frozen graph. The cited text describes H-MG energy exchange behavior but does not define a product-specific quantity, domain, or optimization variable; NIRA dispatch variables from other rules are not reused here without explicit source scope.","empty_theta_reason":"No parameter, coefficient, numeric value, unit, or index set for the local energy product is supplied in this rule's evidence. The cited passage is qualitative and provides no fixed input to formalize as a parameter."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","quote":"several H-MGs, connected to the same network through a market operator or similar platform, can sell their excess energy to adjacent H-MGs or supply their power shortage through neighbours instead of purchasing energy from retailers."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e7c443b591c43af366e9bbf885b058f458cd8caec1138a25bfc6636668a6f2c2","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied evidence defines the local energy product qualitatively as excess energy offered to adjacent H-MGs and energy acquired from neighboring H-MGs to cover shortages. It provides no equation, dispatch variable, parameter, unit, bound, index set, or objective/constraint expression for this product, and the frozen graph contains only the unary node product.local_energy with no edges. This is therefore a procedural market-product definition rather than a supported mathematical rule. The evidence remains unreviewed candidate support.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is the rule's procedural product definition, and the frozen graph provides the unary product.local_energy node but no edges. No graph relationship is replaced with invented mathematics."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
